From: xPDFSDK team <noreply@xpdfsdk.local>
Date: 2026-05-18
Subject: [PATCH 0009] DeviceN fast TranslateImageLine + pdfium009.* markers

Background
==========
0008 added fast TranslateImageLine overrides for IndexedCS and
SeparationCS, but on the test PDF rendering remained slow with
zero `pdfium.IndexedCS::TranslateImageLine` slices firing. The
trace showed 3368 `pdfium.ColorSpace::TranslateImageLine.baseSlow`
slices -- some other colorspace family is still hitting the slow
base-class virtual-dispatch loop.

The PDF keyword scan (decompressed streams) found:
  /Indexed     6   (covered by 0008)
  /Separation  3   (covered by 0008)
  /DeviceN     2   <-- still slow path
  /Lab         1   (has upstream fast override)
  /Pattern     0   (not in PDF)
  /CalRGB      0
  /CalGray     0

`DeviceN` is the last remaining culprit -- it doesn't have an
upstream fast override and the test PDF declares 2 of them, each
shared across many images.

This patch (0009 -- applies on top of 0003+0004+0005+0007+0008)
================================================================
1. Adds a fast `CPDF_DeviceNCS::TranslateImageLine` override:
   - For N=1 components: build a 256-entry BGR table (768 bytes).
   - For N=2 components: build a 65536-entry BGR table (192 KB).
   - For N>=3 components: fall through to slow base class (table
     would be 256^N entries -- prohibitive for N>=3).
   Table is built lazily on first call by walking every input
   value through the existing slow GetRGB() path once. Output is
   bit-identical to the slow loop.

2. Adds atrace markers (with `pdfium009.` prefix to confirm the
   running binary is the 0009 build):
     pdfium009.DeviceNCS::TranslateImageLine
     pdfium009.CalGrayCS::TranslateImageLine
     pdfium009.CalRGBCS::TranslateImageLine
     pdfium009.LabCS::TranslateImageLine
   The Cal*/Lab markers are diagnostic only (those overrides
   already exist upstream and should be narrow). If any of them
   are unexpectedly wide on the next trace, we know to attack
   that one next.

Verifying which build is on the device
======================================
After vendoring the 0009 build, capture a trace. Search for
`pdfium009.` in the slice list:
  - If `pdfium009.DeviceNCS::TranslateImageLine` shows many wide
    slices -> 0009 binary is running and DeviceN was indeed the
    bottleneck. Render should be fast.
  - If you see ZERO `pdfium009.*` slices, you're running an older
    .so -- the vendor step missed.
  - If `pdfium009.DeviceNCS::TranslateImageLine` slices exist but
    are mostly narrow, AND .baseSlow is still wide, then DeviceN
    is NOT the dominant CS -- look at which `pdfium009.*` marker
    IS wide (likely Lab).

Memory
======
N=1 DeviceN colorspace: 768 bytes table.
N=2 DeviceN colorspace: 192 KB table.
N>=3: no table (falls through to slow path).

Fallback
========
If the table build fails or N>=3, `bgr_lookup_usable_` stays false
and the override calls `CPDF_ColorSpace::TranslateImageLine` (the
slow base class). Never produces wrong output.

---
diff --git a/core/fpdfapi/page/cpdf_colorspace.cpp b/core/fpdfapi/page/cpdf_colorspace.cpp
index f765332..2cc0a35 100644
--- a/core/fpdfapi/page/cpdf_colorspace.cpp
+++ b/core/fpdfapi/page/cpdf_colorspace.cpp
@@ -334,9 +334,32 @@ class CPDF_DeviceNCS final : public CPDF_BasedCS {
                   const CPDF_Array* pArray,
                   std::set<const CPDF_Object*>* pVisited) override;
 
+  // xPDFSDK 0009: fast TranslateImageLine override for DeviceN. The
+  // 0007 trace confirmed all baseSlow firings are likely DeviceN-driven
+  // (the only remaining CS family in the test PDF that doesn't have an
+  // upstream fast override). For N=1 or N=2 we precompute a BGR lookup
+  // table once at first use (256 or 65,536 entries * 3 bytes). For N>=3
+  // we fall back to the slow base class -- table size 256^N is
+  // prohibitive. Bit-identical to the slow path.
+  void TranslateImageLine(pdfium::span<uint8_t> dest_span,
+                          pdfium::span<const uint8_t> src_span,
+                          int pixels,
+                          int image_width,
+                          int image_height,
+                          bool bTransMask) const override;
+
  private:
   CPDF_DeviceNCS();
 
+  // xPDFSDK 0009: precomputed BGR table for N=1 or N=2.
+  // N=1: 256 * 3 = 768 bytes. Index = src[i].
+  // N=2: 256 * 256 * 3 = 192 KB. Index = src[i*2]*256 + src[i*2+1].
+  void BuildBgrLookupTableIfNeeded() const;
+  mutable DataVector<uint8_t> bgr_lookup_;
+  mutable bool bgr_lookup_built_ = false;
+  mutable bool bgr_lookup_usable_ = false;
+  mutable uint32_t bgr_lookup_components_ = 0;
+
   std::unique_ptr<const CPDF_Function> func_;
 };
 
@@ -784,6 +807,8 @@ void CPDF_CalGray::TranslateImageLine(pdfium::span<uint8_t> dest_span,
                                       int image_width,
                                       int image_height,
                                       bool bTransMask) const {
+  // xPDFSDK 0009: marker (existing upstream fast path; should be narrow).
+  XPDF_ATRACE_SCOPED("pdfium009.CalGrayCS::TranslateImageLine");
   CHECK(!bTransMask);  // Only applies to CMYK colorspaces.
 
   auto gray_span = src_span.first(static_cast<size_t>(pixels));
@@ -867,6 +892,8 @@ void CPDF_CalRGB::TranslateImageLine(pdfium::span<uint8_t> dest_span,
                                      int image_width,
                                      int image_height,
                                      bool bTransMask) const {
+  // xPDFSDK 0009: marker (existing upstream fast path; should be narrow).
+  XPDF_ATRACE_SCOPED("pdfium009.CalRGBCS::TranslateImageLine");
   CHECK(!bTransMask);  // Only applies to CMYK colorspaces.
   fxcodec::ReverseRGB(dest_span, src_span, pixels);
 }
@@ -958,6 +985,8 @@ void CPDF_LabCS::TranslateImageLine(pdfium::span<uint8_t> dest_span,
                                     int image_width,
                                     int image_height,
                                     bool bTransMask) const {
+  // xPDFSDK 0009: marker on the existing upstream Lab fast override.
+  XPDF_ATRACE_SCOPED("pdfium009.LabCS::TranslateImageLine");
   CHECK(!bTransMask);  // Only applies to CMYK colorspaces.
 
   auto bgr_span = fxcrt::reinterpret_span<FX_BGR_STRUCT<uint8_t>>(dest_span);
@@ -1397,3 +1426,94 @@ std::optional<FX_RGB_STRUCT<float>> CPDF_DeviceNCS::GetRGB(
   }
   return base_cs_->GetRGB(results);
 }
+
+// xPDFSDK 0009: precompute BGR table for DeviceN. For N=1, build a
+// 256-entry table indexed by the single source byte. For N=2, build
+// a 65536-entry table indexed by (src[0]*256 + src[1]). For N>=3,
+// the table is too large -- leave bgr_lookup_usable_ false and fall
+// back to the slow base class path. Bit-identical to the slow loop:
+// each table entry is exactly what GetRGBOrZerosOnError would compute
+// per pixel.
+void CPDF_DeviceNCS::BuildBgrLookupTableIfNeeded() const {
+  if (bgr_lookup_built_) {
+    return;
+  }
+  bgr_lookup_built_ = true;
+
+  const uint32_t n = ComponentCount();
+  bgr_lookup_components_ = n;
+  if (n < 1 || n > 2) {
+    return;  // N>=3 -> table too big; fall through to base class.
+  }
+
+  const size_t n_entries = (n == 1) ? 256u : 256u * 256u;
+  bgr_lookup_ = DataVector<uint8_t>(n_entries * 3);
+
+  std::vector<float> src_f(n, 0.0f);
+  for (size_t idx = 0; idx < n_entries; ++idx) {
+    if (n == 1) {
+      src_f[0] = static_cast<float>(idx) / 255.0f;
+    } else {
+      // N=2: idx = c0 * 256 + c1
+      src_f[0] = static_cast<float>(idx >> 8) / 255.0f;
+      src_f[1] = static_cast<float>(idx & 0xff) / 255.0f;
+    }
+    auto rgb_opt = GetRGB(pdfium::span<const float>(src_f.data(), src_f.size()));
+    if (!rgb_opt.has_value()) {
+      bgr_lookup_[idx * 3 + 0] = 0;
+      bgr_lookup_[idx * 3 + 1] = 0;
+      bgr_lookup_[idx * 3 + 2] = 0;
+      continue;
+    }
+    const auto& rgb = rgb_opt.value();
+    bgr_lookup_[idx * 3 + 0] =
+        static_cast<uint8_t>(std::clamp(rgb.blue, 0.0f, 1.0f) * 255);
+    bgr_lookup_[idx * 3 + 1] =
+        static_cast<uint8_t>(std::clamp(rgb.green, 0.0f, 1.0f) * 255);
+    bgr_lookup_[idx * 3 + 2] =
+        static_cast<uint8_t>(std::clamp(rgb.red, 0.0f, 1.0f) * 255);
+  }
+  bgr_lookup_usable_ = true;
+}
+
+void CPDF_DeviceNCS::TranslateImageLine(pdfium::span<uint8_t> dest_span,
+                                        pdfium::span<const uint8_t> src_span,
+                                        int pixels,
+                                        int image_width,
+                                        int image_height,
+                                        bool bTransMask) const {
+  // xPDFSDK 0009: marker prefix `pdfium009.` so we can see in the
+  // Perfetto trace that the 0009 binary is actually running. If this
+  // slice doesn't appear after vendoring, the device has an older .so.
+  XPDF_ATRACE_SCOPED("pdfium009.DeviceNCS::TranslateImageLine");
+
+  BuildBgrLookupTableIfNeeded();
+  if (!bgr_lookup_usable_) {
+    // N >= 3 or build failure -> base class slow path.
+    CPDF_ColorSpace::TranslateImageLine(dest_span, src_span, pixels,
+                                        image_width, image_height, bTransMask);
+    return;
+  }
+
+  const uint8_t* src = src_span.data();
+  uint8_t* dst = dest_span.data();
+  const uint8_t* table = bgr_lookup_.data();
+
+  if (bgr_lookup_components_ == 1) {
+    for (int i = 0; i < pixels; ++i) {
+      const uint8_t* entry = &table[src[i] * 3];
+      dst[i * 3 + 0] = entry[0];
+      dst[i * 3 + 1] = entry[1];
+      dst[i * 3 + 2] = entry[2];
+    }
+  } else {  // N == 2
+    for (int i = 0; i < pixels; ++i) {
+      const size_t idx = static_cast<size_t>(src[i * 2]) * 256u +
+                         static_cast<size_t>(src[i * 2 + 1]);
+      const uint8_t* entry = &table[idx * 3];
+      dst[i * 3 + 0] = entry[0];
+      dst[i * 3 + 1] = entry[1];
+      dst[i * 3 + 2] = entry[2];
+    }
+  }
+}

